      "id": "yugioh-card-back",
      "kind": "photo",
      "title": "Yu-Gi-Oh! card back",
      "by": "Konami / Kazuki Takahashi",
      "year": 1999,
      "note": "\"wow, this is design, remarkable.\" The one image every player saw thousands of times: a black oval pulled into a whirlpool of molten orange and gold flow lines, marbled and slightly moire, inside a grainy burnt-orange border. It is the same on every card, so it works as a seal, not an illustration. Shares the concentric-ring language of the wash ripples, but dark, hot and high-contrast.",
